      "writtenOn": "2017-12-01T08:41:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the spec in section 4.4 COMMAND FLOW CONTROL, it say:\n\n\"To indicate to the Host that the Controller is ready to receive HCI command packets, the Controller may generate a Command Complete or Command Status event with the Command Opcode set to 0x0000 and the Num HCI Command Packets event parameter set to 1 or more.\"\n\nSo we should also consider a command status event with zero opcode as a NOP.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 288,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "ebe4a5ceaf88dbeeebf2fe7077fd4d59bd0661e9",
